      <activity id="7ef51232-e26b-55c0-aaf9-88c0fe2c4285" activityNameId="617f182a-2cd7-5da7-b2da-9c74835063de" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, building, window frame, wood-metal, opaquely painted, m2 visible, to final disposal</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, building, window frame, wood-metal, opaquely painted, m2 visible, to final disposal
The amount of materials to be disposed of at the end of life was estimated based on the bill of materials. A cut-off approach is used for recycling of metals (aluminium and zinc). The functional unit is 1m2 of visible area.;
UUID: 081d2c64-1bf6-492f-9796-8c613a567ab7
Included processes are the disposal of wood, glue, steel, plastics, paint, rubber. The transport to the municipal incineration plant is included.
Location: Data apply to the supply in Switzerland.
Technology: Industry data.
Time period: Time of publications
Production volume: na
Sampling: Data survey at 4 window manufacturers in Switzerland. 
Extrapolations: Some generic datasets from ecoinvent have been used.
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_081d2c64-1bf6-492f-9796-8c613a567ab7.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
